course: dictionary
lesson: 8122
title: Repeatedly: again and again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Repeatedly means many times, again and again. It is an adverb, so it tells us how often something happens. «The dog barked repeatedly.» The dog did not bark just once. It kept on barking, over and over.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Stir repeatedly» in a recipe means keep stirring, not stir once and stop. The clues here are stir and the instruction itself, so you can tell that repeatedly means more than one time.
explain: Words can change how a sentence feels, but repeatedly is clear. «Character thinking says we become what we repeatedly do.» Repeatedly points to actions we do many times. Swap in many times and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Maths uses the same idea. Multiplication is repeated addition, so 5 × 2 means 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2. Repeated subtraction works the same way when you take away the same number again and again.
fact: Repeatedly means many times, again and again.
fact: Repeatedly is an adverb, so it tells us how often an action happens.
fact: Similar words and phrases are again and again, over and over, and many times.
fact: Multiplication is repeated addition: 5 × 2 is 2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2.
fact: A good check is to swap in many times and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The dog barked repeatedly.» What does repeatedly mean? | *Many times, again and again | Once, very loudly | Quietly, in a whisper | Sadly, with its tail down
exercise: Which phrase means the same as repeatedly? | *Over and over | Far away | Only once | At the very end
exercise: Multiplication is repeated addition. Which sum shows 5 × 2? | 10 - 2 | 2 + 5 | 5 + 5 | *2 + 2 + 2 + 2 + 2
test: «Stir repeatedly.» What should you do? | Pour it out | Stop stirring at once | Stir once and stop | *Keep stirring, again and again
test: «We become what we repeatedly do.» What does repeatedly show? | Things we do only once | Things we do very quickly | Things we never do | *Things we do many times, over and over
exam: «Aristotle said we become what we repeatedly do.» What does repeatedly mean here? | Without any thought at all | Only once, at the start | *Many times, again and again | Very quickly and loudly
